Companion to 01776ef (the LLM modal save-wipe fix). User asked to
mirror the first-time setup wizard's "verify key + fetch models" flow
into the Profile → Change modal so they don't have to type model names
blind.

Implementation is a straight port from setup/+page.svelte:
- Same state shape (keyValidating, keyValid, keyError, availableModels).
- Same call: setup.validateKey(provider, key, baseUrl?). The endpoint
  /api/setup/validate-key already returns { valid, error?, models }
  via routes/setup.rs::fetch_provider_models, which calls upstream
  /v1/models with the right header (x-api-key for anthropic,
  Authorization for openai-compatible).
- Validate button rendered only when provider is openai/anthropic
  (matches setup; ollama validation isn't supported by that endpoint
  and there's a separate detect_ollama path).

One deviation from setup: when validate succeeds and returns models,
setup conditionally renders either a <select> or a free-text <input>
based on whether the model field was set. The modal here ALWAYS shows
a model field (it's editing an existing agent), so I render a <select>
post-validation but seed it with a "<model> (custom)" option at the
top if the agent's stored model isn't in the fetched list. This
preserves relay-specific or fine-tuned model names that the upstream's
/v1/models doesn't expose. Without that, switching to the dropdown
silently changes the bind:value to the first option in the list, which
would have been a quieter version of the same data-loss class as the
bug we just fixed.

Reset semantics: keyValid/keyError/availableModels reset every time
the modal opens AND every time the provider changes (onchange on the
provider <select>). User explicitly asked for "reset on open" in
scoping. Provider-change reset isn't a separate user ask but is
necessary — a green "valid" status from openai shouldn't persist after
the user switches to anthropic.

Things I considered and rejected:
- <datalist> autocomplete instead of a hard switch to <select>. Would
  give free-text + suggestions in one widget. Rejected to match the
  setup UX faithfully (user said "match setup", which uses <select>).
- Auto-validate on modal open when api_key is populated. Setup doesn't,
  and the user agreed "match setup". Avoids hitting upstream every
  time someone opens the modal to glance at config.
- A new backend route for validation scoped to existing agents. The
  existing /api/setup/validate-key works for the use case (it's
  stateless — doesn't depend on the agent record), so no reason to
  duplicate. Slight smell that a "setup" endpoint is being used post-
  setup; left a follow-up note in my head to move it to a neutral
  namespace if the surface grows.

Verified: cargo build of the desktop installer green (build.ps1
--skip-test --skip-docker --skip-check), svelte-check 0 errors,
manual test against the relay (relay.public.cloud.xpress.ai) — Validate
button fires, status shows, models populate, custom model preserved
across opens.

